; Tutorial_1_User_Interface.inix -- the window, the record list, the Say keys, the menus, the key rules, and help.

[about]
Title=1 - User Interface
Intro=How DbDo is laid out and how its keys are chosen, shown in RadioTrail: rows and columns, the Say keys, the menus, the rules behind every key, and the four places help lives.
Setup=DbDo is open on RadioTrail.
Homework=Press Shift plus Z in any table, and Alt plus F10 whenever a key will not come to mind.

[step]

Say=DbDo is heard before it is seen. I name each part; the reader shows it.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Alt plus Control plus D, D for DbDo, opens it or brings it forward.
Key=Alt+Control+D
Hear=DbDo
Hear=DbDo ready

[step]

Say=The main view is a list of records. Down Arrow moves by row, and the reader speaks the record: here, a station's name, its genres and its country.
Key=Down Arrow
Hear=!MODA, dance, electronic, house, Spain, Row 2 of 55280
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Right Arrow moves by column within the record, saying the column's name and its value.
Key=Right Arrow
Hear=genre, dance, electronic, house, pop en espanol e ingles, top hits
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Now the Say keys. Shift and a letter asks, and changes nothing. Shift plus Z is Say Status.
Key=Shift+Z
Hear=stations, 55280 records, no filter, sorted by name
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Table, count, filter and sort in one breath. Shift plus C, C for Cell, says the cell you are on.
Key=Shift+C
Hear=genre, dance, electronic, house, pop en espanol e ingles, top hits
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Shift plus Y, Say Yield, says how many records are in view; Shift plus 8 says the sort and filter.
Key=Shift+8
Hear=Sort: name. Filter: none.
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Where a field has fixed values, Control plus F2, Pick Value, offers them as a list, so nothing is mistyped. On the country column:
Key=Control+F2
Hear=country: list box, Spain
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=A letter jumps to a value. Escape closes the list and changes nothing. F10 opens the menu bar.
Key=F10
Hear=Menu bar
Hear=File menu

[step]

Say=Down Arrow to the first item.
Key=Down Arrow
Hear=Open Database..., Control plus O, O
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=The item, its key, then its letter: learn a key from the menu once, then skip the menu.
Key=Escape
Hear=Leaving menus

[step]

Say=The rules behind every key. A letter is the first letter of a word: Control plus O opens, Alt plus O orders. Control does; Shift asks.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Adding Shift reverses: Control plus M marks, Control plus Shift plus M unmarks. Z is for sleep, so every Z key is a toggle. And each function key is a family: F2 edits, F3 searches again, F4 lists the windows open.
Key=F4
Hear=Current Windows dialog, RadioTrail, stations, 1 of 1
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Escape. Control plus F1 is the Key Describer: each key says what it does instead of doing it.
Key=Control+F1
Hear=Key Describer On

[step]

Say=Now Control plus O only describes itself.
Key=Control+O
Hear=Open Database, Control plus O

[step]

Say=Control plus F1 again, and it is off.
Key=Control+F1
Hear=No Key Describer

[step]

Say=When a key will not come to mind, Alt plus F10, the Alternate Menu, lists every command in one list you type into, with its key beside it.
Key=Alt+F10
Hear=Alternate Menu
Hear=Command, list box

[step]

Say=I type the word play, and the list narrows to the commands with that word.
Key=play
Hear=Play Stream, Alt plus Shift plus P
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Escape closes the list without running anything. Help lives in four places, the same in every Homer program. I say which; the reader says the key. The guide.
Key=Escape
Hear=F1

[step]

Say=The changes, release by release.
Key=
Hear=Shift plus F1

[step]

Say=The version.
Key=
Hear=Alt plus F1

[step]

Say=Every key in a window you can search.
Key=
Hear=Alt plus Shift plus H, Hotkey Summary

[step]

Say=What this walk taught. I name the command; the reader gives the key.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Say Status.
Key=
Hear=Shift plus Z

[step]

Say=Pick a field's fixed value.
Key=
Hear=Control plus F2

[step]

Say=Unmark, the reverse of Mark.
Key=
Hear=Control plus Shift plus M

[step]

Say=Every command in one list.
Key=
Hear=Alt plus F10
